    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `locality`), which regenerates `OwnerDto` at build with the new field.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 A small function class mirroring `Locality`. It resolves the owner's region via `Locality.of(customerCode, postcode, city)` and maps it through the fixed table `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`, returning `null` for any other region so the field is simply absent.\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `timezone` calling `Timezone.of(...)` with the same inputs as `locality`, keeping the exposed timezone consistent with the region-and-hash identity.\n\nThe provided `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 `locality` NSW, `timezone` Australia/Sydney) passes, and the full test suite builds green.",
